  "id": "regression-tree",
  "term": "regression tree",
  "definition": "A regression tree is a statistical model used to find which variables are related to an outcome across different participant segments. It does this by splitting the sample into groups using partitioning variables and then examining the associations within those groups; in a mixed-effects form, it can also account for fixed predictors and random differences such as district or survey round.",
